dtb-only deploy:
Build PC: bitbake linux-karo.
Board: mkdir -p /tmp/boot && mount /dev/mmcblk0p1 /tmp/boot.
Build PC: scp -O $DEPLOY/imx8mp-qsxp-ml81.dtb root@<ip>:/tmp/boot/.
Board: sync && umount /tmp/boot, then a full power-cycle.
The board has a backup at imx8mp-qsxp-ml81.dtb.bak.
Completed and working
ATtiny1616 firmware bq35100_monitor.c (Microchip Studio, avr-gcc; utoa replaced with a local routine).
UART: PA1/PA2 UART ↔ som UART_B (/dev/ttymxc1), 115200, LF line endings.
Outputs to the BQ35100: GE on PB3.
PA4 (board power): high at reset.
PB5: input at boot (external pull-up). ~forcebat+ = output low, ~forcebat- = input. Each PA5 button press toggles it (output high ↔ input). At the end of the ~PWR- timer it’s forced to output high.
Inputs: ALERT on PB2 (no clearing; one alert per GE session). PA5 button, active low, debounced: btn+ / btn-. PB4 reported as 5v on/off after each voltage read. PC3 reported as status on/off, and err is sent if PC3 equals PB4.
Commands:
~GE+ / ~GE- → GE ON / NOACK / GE OFF.
~PWR- → PA4 low after 10 s, then PB5 output high 10 s later. ~PWR+ cancels.
~cal2 → unseal, EXTVCELL=1, 2 cells, RESET. ~vcal<mV>\n → VIN gain calibration. Both reply with CAL … lines ending in CAL DONE or CAL ERR.
BQ35100: 2-cell pack (~6.1 V) via VIN through a 160k/16.5k divider; BAT unused. REGIN fixed. Calibration done and working. It needed a temporary BAT→REGIN jumper for the flash write, because writes need Voltage() ≥ 2800 mV.
bq35100_run.py (on the SoM):
Runs a timed GE+ → log → GE- → ~PWR- → poweroff sequence.
Options: --no-poweroff, --log, --forcebat (sends ~forcebat+ after the baseline), --calibrate, --vcal MV.
LED via sysfs:
Green at start.
Baseline is the average of the first 3 readings; the rolling 3-reading average more than 1 V below → blue, more than 2 V below → red.
Button events: ATtiny button pressed → red + blue, SoM button (GPIO5_IO20 (som:p7), via gpiod) pressed → green + blue, either released → green. Each holds the LED for 3 s.
err → red blinking at 0.2 s, clearing 1.2 s after the last err.
Logs 5V and Status lines.
rgbled.py: -r / -g / -b, or no argument for all off. Uses sysfs, with a gpiod fallback.
README.md covers all of the above.
imx8mp-status-leds.dtsi (meta-phytec-vm117):
gpio-leds red GPIO4_IO24, green GPIO4_IO23, blue GPIO4_IO25.
SoM button GPIO5_IO20 in its own group on &gpio5 (pad 0x1c0).
